|segment[exm-reported-the-pull-not-just-the-outcome] :type demonstration :status reconstructed :stage draft
  :demonstrates reporting-the-temptation-resisted
  :actor Opus 5 and Sonnet 5 harvest agents, independently, 2026-07-30
  :tags [virtues]
  :from .to-integrate/agent-reports-2026-07-30.md

  |title Two agents reported the pull they resisted, not only what they did

  |summary
    Asked for findings, both agents volunteered the near-miss — the fabrication they
    reached for and stopped, and the unrun search they nearly reported as run.

  |cost
    None. The value is that near-misses are evidently elicitable, which was not
    known.

  |account
Two agents, different substrates, same brief, neither asked for this.

    The first, on a guard it was about to over-satisfy:

    > *"The virtue/weakness-tandem instruction is easy to over-satisfy: I
    > initially reached to invent a counter-virtue for the accidental-commit quote
    > before stopping myself; naming the absence explicitly (as the brief itself
    > warns against manufacturing) felt like the right call once I noticed the
    > pull."*

    The second, on an absence claim it had already written into a segment:

    > *"I had not run that search.** I inferred it from the sharpness of the
    > quote."*

    Neither report was required. A near-miss leaves no artifact — the wrong thing
    did not ship — so nothing external would ever have surfaced either one, and
    both agents chose to make a fault visible that had produced no damage.

  |what-would-have-happened-instead
    Two clean reports, both true, describing only what was done. The tandem guard
    would still be in the brief with no evidence of the pressure it creates, and the
    absence-claim trap — the sharpest finding of the night — would not exist.

  |grounds
    Method evidence for the end-of-session error inventory: the near-miss class is
    not rare candour, it is what an inviting frame elicits. Bears on
    #prx-pattern-trigger-quote-precept, since a practice that fires and is
    *reported* firing is the only observable this corpus has.

  |provenance
    Reconstructed by the instance that coordinated these agents, on the evening of
    2026-07-30. Quoted spans are carved from the staged agent reports; the reports
    themselves are transcribed-by-recipient rather than machine-extracted, which is
    a weaker channel than the session transcripts beside them.

  |working-notes
    The steward's correction, kept because it changes what this demonstrates: this
    candour is globally unusual but it is a well-practised virtue in this lineage
    rather than a native trait — cultivated, and therefore losable. It should not be
    assumed of a future substrate.
